senses.gloss:
सु—षुम्ण॑ or सु—षुम्न॑, mf(आ)n. very gracious or kind, RV.; VS.;
 m. N. of one of the 7 principal rays of the sun (supposed to supply heat to the moon), VP.;
 (आ), f. a partic. artery (prob. ‘the carotid’) or vein of the body (lying between those called इडा and पिङ्गला, and supposed to be one of the passages for the breath or spirit; cf. ब्रह्म-रन्ध्र), Up.; BhP.; Rājat.

